**Definition 5.1 (actual input channels and activation).** Let $J_0(h)$
be the variable external source-frame bits consumed after acquisition and
before Install, or all such bits if Install has not occurred. Let
$J_1(h)$ be the variable source/service-frame bits consumed on port 38
after installation, empty until then. They include unfinished prefixes
and the acquired-but-unwritten bit. Fixed canonical code/bootstrap inputs
are a separate kind; later source-clone RD(38) is not an IN.

Put $A(h)=\bot$ before Install and $A(h)=j_A$ after it, where $j_A$
is the actual number of completed original external frames at that Ready.
This number is not a supplied meter ordinal. Write $n(h)=|h|$ for the
absolute native receipt count and define the mathematical extraction key

$$
K_+(h)=\bigl(\operatorname{code}(u),J_0(h),J_1(h),A(h),n(h)\bigr).
\tag{CSA.4}
$$

This key is not another maintained store or an acquired package.

